error[NK2120]: This `async` stands inside a loop's body, but `async` starts only tasks whose number stands in the source.
  --> tests/async_parse_inside_a_loop_is_refused.nika:7:3
   |
 7 | 		let h = async(detached) fn { println("in a for") }
   |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A loop would start one task each time round, and a group's tasks are counted where they are written.
   = help: To run the body for every element beside the others, write `xs.par_iter().for_each fn(x) { … }`.
error[NK2120]: This `async` stands inside a loop's body, but `async` starts only tasks whose number stands in the source.
   --> tests/async_parse_inside_a_loop_is_refused.nika:14:4
    |
 14 | 			async(detached) fn { println("in a while") }.join()
    |    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: A loop would start one task each time round, and a group's tasks are counted where they are written.
    = help: To run the body for every element beside the others, write `xs.par_iter().for_each fn(x) { … }`.
warning[NK2123]: `spawn` is replaced by `async(detached)`, which starts the same task.
   --> tests/async_parse_inside_a_loop_is_refused.nika:21:3
    |
 21 | 		spawn fn { println("spawned") }.join()
    |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `spawn fn { … }` is the earlier spelling of `async(detached) fn { … }` (ADR-async-5 D13); it is removed once every use is rewritten.
    = help: `async(detached)` is refused inside a loop's body (`NK2120`): to run the body for every element beside the others, write `xs.par_iter().for_each fn(x) { … }`.

